# # /amrf/
#
# AMRF (AntiMicrobial Resistance Framework): a vocabulary to describe
# antimicrobial resistance prediction models and the processing steps that
# prepare their inputs, so that a framework can discover which models can be
# applied to a sample. Developed as part of Cocos:
# https://github.com/DEAL-US/Cocos
#
# https://w3id.org/amrf/shapes redirects to the SHACL shapes; everything else
# under https://w3id.org/amrf/ (the vocabulary and its terms) redirects to the
# vocabulary, both in Turtle.
#
# ## Contact
# This space is administered by:
#
# María Quirós Quiroga
# mquiros1@us.es
# GitHub username: mquirosq
#
# Daniel Ayala Hernández
# dayala1@us.es
# GitHub username: dayala1
#
# Fernando Sola Espinosa
# fsola@us.es
# GitHub username: fersolesp

RewriteEngine on

RewriteRule ^shapes$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DEAL-US/Cocos/main/app/semantics/vocab/shapes.ttl [R=303,L]
RewriteRule ^.*$ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DEAL-US/Cocos/main/app/semantics/vocab/amrf.ttl [R=303,L]
